The discovered `BranchSession` is not the required fork: it selects a branch inside the same Keith session/root and therefore shares ordering and cancellation. Advertising that as ACP `session/fork` would violate the official contract’s “new independent session” semantics and the task’s own concurrency requirement, so I will not wire a false capability. I’m now inventorying the existing ACP fixtures and the real daemon-process harness to add the remaining honest coverage while keeping the independent-fork gap explicit.
