I found and am correcting one ACP-owned durability bug independent of the unavailable SDK: recovery currently treats any historical user message with identical text as proof that the current in-flight prompt committed. That can silently drop a legitimate repeated prompt. Keith already has durable command-ID prompt ingress, so recovery should always replay the same stored command ID and let the daemon’s real idempotency ledger decide.
